# Virtual Tour Manager — Dropdown Menu Item

**Date:** 2026-06-02
**Branch:** master
**Status:** Approved

## Overview

Add a "Virtual Tour Manager" item to the Virtual Tour dropdown on each tour card in My Tours. Clicking it navigates the user to the existing Virtual Tour Manager page (`/my-tours/:mid/hosted`) using internal React Router navigation.

## Affected File

`src/components/organism/ListTour/VirtualTourDropdown.jsx`

## Placement

The new item is appended as the **last entry** in the `DropdownMenu`, after the existing "Edit Virtual Tour" item.

Final menu order:

| # | Item | Condition |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | View Virtual Tour | `item.overlay_active` |
| 2 | View Google Virtual Tour | `item.goverlay_active` |
| 3 | Edit Virtual Tour | always shown |
| 4 | Virtual Tour Manager | always shown (new) |

## Navigation

Uses `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom` to navigate internally to `/my-tours/${item.mid}/hosted`. This is an SPA transition — no full page reload.

The target route `/my-tours/:mid/hosted` already exists in `src/routes/myTours.js` (line 44) and renders `src/pages/Tour/Detail/Hosted/HostedTour/HostedTour.jsx`.

## Component Change

`VirtualTourDropdown.jsx` gains:
- `useNavigate` import from `react-router-dom`
- One new `DropdownItem` at the bottom of `DropdownMenu`

```jsx
import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom';

// inside component:
const navigate = useNavigate();

// last DropdownItem in DropdownMenu:
<DropdownItem
  key="manager"
  color="default"
  onPress={() => {
    navigate(`/my-tours/${item.mid}/hosted`);
  }}
>
  {t('t_my_tours.t_virtual_tour_dropdown.t_manager')}
</DropdownItem>
```

## Localization

One new key added to all 18 locale files after the existing `t_my_tours.t_virtual_tour_dropdown` sibling keys:

| Key | Value (EN) |
|---|---|
| `t_my_tours.t_virtual_tour_dropdown.t_manager` | `"Virtual Tour Manager"` |

English string is used as the initial value for all non-English locales.

## What Does NOT Change

- No new components, hooks, or routes
- No changes to `TourCard.jsx`, `ToursTable.jsx`, or `List.jsx`
- The existing "Edit Virtual Tour" item (external overlay editor) is untouched
- The `VirtualTourDropdown` visibility logic (`overlay_active || goverlay_active`) in the parent is untouched
